# Neo Arp parameters (docs/specs/neo-arp.md). The order changes only with a version (machines.md §3.2): songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoArp
namespace NeoBuzz.Arp
class NeoArpMachine
summary An arpeggiator that works on note wires: it takes the notes you hold (or a chord from another note machine) and sends them on one at a time, in time with the song. Twelve patterns (up, down, up-down, converge, diverge, as played, random, random walk, a whole chord, or your own 16-step row with ties, accents and a transpose per step), a rate from 1/1 to 1/64 with dotted and triplet or a free time in milliseconds, swing, gate, one to four octaves, repeats, velocity, humanize and a latch. It makes no sound itself: put it before a synth as a note insert, or on a note wire to any machine that takes notes. Use it for arpeggios, rhythmic chord stabs, basslines and sequenced leads.

group Pattern
Pattern     "Pattern"        0 11 0     enum Up Down Up-down Up-down_ends_twice Down-up Converge Diverge As_played Random Random_walk Chord Steps | The order the held notes are played in
    id pattern
    how Chooses the order the held notes are played in: up, down, back and forth, from the outside in or the inside out, as you played them, at random, as a walk, all together as a chord, or by your own step row.
    sound Up and Down make runs, Up-down a wave, Converge and Diverge a pinch or a bloom, Random a sparkle, Chord a rhythmic pulse and Steps a sequenced line.
Octaves     "Octaves"        1 4 1      int 0                                | How many octaves the pattern climbs through (1 … 4)
    id octaves
    how Plays the pattern again an octave higher, up to four octaves, in the order the Octave mode says.
    sound More octaves widen the run: a sweeping arpeggio instead of a close figure.
OctMode     "Octave mode"    0 2 0      enum Up Down Up-down                 | The order the octaves are visited in
    id octave_mode
    how Chooses whether each pass of the pattern goes up an octave, down an octave or up and back down.
    sound Up climbs away, Down falls toward the played notes, Up-down rises and returns.
Repeats     "Repeats"        1 4 1      int 0                                | How many times each note is played before the next (1 … 4)
    id repeats
    how Plays each note of the pattern this many times in a row before moving on.
    sound Higher values make the figure stutter on each note: a pulsing, slower-moving arpeggio.
Transpose   "Transpose"      0 48 24    int -24 st signed                    | Moves every note by semitones (−24 … +24)
    id transpose
    how Moves every note up or down by this many semitones.
    sound It shifts the whole arpeggio without changing the keys you hold.

group Rate
Sync        "Timing"         0 1 0      enum Song_tempo Free_time            | Whether steps follow the song's tempo or run on a time in milliseconds
    id timing
    how Chooses between steps locked to the song's tempo and position and steps of a fixed length in milliseconds.
    sound Song tempo keeps the arpeggio in time with the music; Free time runs at its own speed, whatever the tempo.
Rate        "Rate"           0 6 4      enum 1/1 1/2 1/4 1/8 1/16 1/32 1/64  | The length of a step at the song's tempo
    id rate
    how Sets how long each step lasts at the song's tempo, from a whole note to a sixty-fourth.
    sound Shorter steps make a faster, busier arpeggio.
Feel        "Feel"           0 2 0      enum Straight Dotted Triplet         | Straight, dotted (1.5 times as long) or triplet (two thirds as long) steps
    id feel
    how Makes the steps straight, dotted (one and a half times as long) or triplet (two thirds as long).
    sound Dotted steps lilt against the beat; triplets make a rolling, three-against-two feel.
FreeMs      "Free time"      20 2000 125 lin 20 2000 ms 0                            | The length of a step in milliseconds when Timing is Free time (20 … 2000)
    id free_time
    how Sets the length of a step in milliseconds when Timing is Free time.
    sound Shorter times are faster; the pattern no longer follows the song's tempo.
Swing       "Swing"          0 75 0     int 0 %                              | Delays every second step by up to 75 % of a step
    id swing
    how Delays every second step by a share of a step, up to 75 %.
    sound The arpeggio takes a shuffled, off-beat lilt.

group Gate
Gate        "Gate"           5 200 80   int 0 %                             | How long each note lasts, as a share of a step (5 … 200 %)
    id gate
    how Sets how long each note sounds as a share of one step; above 100 % the notes overlap.
    sound Low values are short and detached; 100 % just touches the next note; higher values run together, legato.

group Velocity
VelMode     "Velocity"       0 2 0      enum As_played Fixed Accent         | Where the velocity of each note comes from
    id velocity_mode
    how Chooses the velocity: as you played each key, one fixed value, or a fixed value with the accented steps louder.
    sound As played keeps your touch; Fixed makes every note equally loud; Accent makes the marked steps stand out.
FixedVel    "Fixed velocity" 1 127 100  int 0                                | The velocity of Fixed and Accent modes (1 … 127)
    id fixed_velocity
    how Sets the velocity used by the Fixed and Accent modes.
    sound Higher values play every note harder and brighter on most instruments.
AccentLevel "Accent"         0 100 60   int 0 %                              | How far an accented step rises above the fixed velocity, toward 127
    id accent_level
    how Sets how far an accented step lifts the velocity from the fixed value toward 127 (Accent mode, Steps pattern).
    sound Higher values make the accented steps hit harder.
HumTime     "Humanize time"  0 20 0     lin 0 20 ms 0                             | Random lateness of each note, up to this many milliseconds
    id humanize_time
    how Delays each note by a random time up to this many milliseconds, the same every time the song is played.
    sound A little looseness takes the machine-like edge off the pattern.
HumVel      "Humanize velocity" 0 30 0  int 0 %                              | Random change of each note's velocity, up to this share
    id humanize_velocity
    how Changes each note's velocity by a random amount up to this share, the same every time the song is played.
    sound A little variation makes repeated notes feel played, not stamped.

group Hold
Latch       "Latch"          0 1 0      switch                               | Keeps the notes sounding after you let go, until you play a new chord
    id latch
    how With Latch on, the notes stay in the arpeggio after release until a new chord is played.
    sound You can take your hands off and the arpeggio keeps going.
Retrigger   "Retrigger"      0 2 0      enum Free_running On_new_note On_bar | When the pattern starts over
    id retrigger
    how Chooses when the pattern restarts: never (it follows the song position), on each new note, or on each bar line; steps always stay on the song's grid.
    sound Free running keeps the pattern in step with the song wherever you start; the others always begin the figure from its first note.

group Steps
StepLen     "Step count"     1 16 16    int 0                                | How many steps of the row the Steps pattern uses (1 … 16)
    id step_count
    how Sets how many of the 16 steps the Steps pattern plays before it starts over.
    sound Counts that do not divide the bar make the pattern drift against it.
S1          "Step 1"        0 3 1      enum Off On Tie Accent               | Step 1 of the row: Off, On, Tie (holds the note before it) or Accent
    how Sets what step 1 of the row does in the Steps pattern: rest (Off), play a note (On), hold the note before it (Tie) or play it louder (Accent).
    sound Ties lengthen a note across steps and accents make the marked steps stand out, which is what gives the row its rhythm.
S2          "Step 2"        0 3 1      enum Off On Tie Accent               | Step 2 of the row: Off, On, Tie (holds the note before it) or Accent
    how Sets what step 2 of the row does in the Steps pattern: rest (Off), play a note (On), hold the note before it (Tie) or play it louder (Accent).
    sound Ties lengthen a note across steps and accents make the marked steps stand out, which is what gives the row its rhythm.
